A||N||4||westtexas||Which computer/harness is used for 4.9 swap?||||1||
Z||000000||westtexas||05-30-2001||06:41 PM||||There is '91 Caddy 4.9 with 106 K in a salvage yard nearby for $700(is that a good price?). The '91 has MPI. From what I understand BubbaJoe uses an '88-'89 computer which controls a DFI (throttle body injection?). I'm really confused here. Which harness and which fuel injection should I use? I need to go to the wrecking yard knowing what I need to buy. This may be obvious to most of you and that's why I'm asking. Thanks for any help, Robert.<BR> <P>------------------<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000001||85blackgt||05-30-2001||06:48 PM||||you will need the harness from the car you got the 4.9 from and the computer system!||||reg||1
Z||000002||pherder||05-30-2001||07:57 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by 85blackgt:<BR><B>you will need the harness from the car you got the 4.9 from and the computer system!</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>The problem with the 90+ system is that there are two computers!!  Both must be used and hooked up to the equipment on the Caddy to make it work in anything but limp home mode.<P>Unfortuneately, the Fiero doesn't have all the systems that the Caddy has and from what I have read, you can't fake the computer out without rewriting the code.<P>One solution is to put on the 4.9 an earlier TBI setup and the TPI's computer.  <P>Another solution is to go to an aftermarket system like the Holley 950 or something like the Haltech E6GM computer.<P> <A HREF="http://www.haltech.com.au/Products/ECUs/E6GM/e6gm.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.haltech.com.au/Products/ECUs/E6GM/e6gm.html</A> <P>The normal cost for this computer is $695.  I have one for sale for $600 that is brand new and unused if you are interested.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>Paul<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000003||PBJ||05-30-2001||08:18 PM|||| <A HREF="http://members.fortunecity.com/bubbajoexx/" TARGET=_blank>http://members.fortunecity.com/bubbajoexx/</A> <P>You have seen this page before I hope.  I have emailed Joe a few times and is a great guy for help and getting back to you.  He has suggested to me that if you are putting in a 4.9 use the intake and tbi and computer from 4.5 on the 4.9 otherwise just get a 4.5L.  The 4.9 is bigger but needs to be bigger for emissions reasons to get the same results and a bit better than previous 4.5.  If you want more power out of a 4.X mtr than see Joe's dist conversion and carb set up.||||reg||1
Z||000004||westtexas||05-30-2001||08:58 PM||||Your information is the kind I need. Yes, I have been to BubbaJoe's web page many times but some things aren't easy for me to understand. Hit me between the eyes and I get it. BubbaJoe has answered a couple of my questions but I'm guessing he has too emails to spend much time on each one. I appreciate the offer of the Haltech chip. I'm trying to this swap cheap. It's going in a plain '87 2.5 (blown) auto. If this works I'll try a swap into my '86 GT 4-speed. On that one I'll spend money. So, I'm going to look for a '88-'89 4.5L and the distributor BubbaJoe mentioned. Thanks for straigtening me out. Robert||||reg||1
